# Phase 6: Project Documentation Phase

## Project Title: EduGenie – Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant

### 1. Introduction

The Project Documentation Phase focuses on preparing complete technical and user documentation for the EduGenie application. Documentation provides detailed information about the project objectives, system requirements, architecture, development process, testing procedures, and usage instructions.

It helps developers, evaluators, and users understand how the application is designed, developed, and operated.

### 2. Objectives of Documentation

1. To provide a complete overview of the EduGenie project.

2. To document functional and non-functional requirements.

3. To explain the system architecture and workflow.

4. To describe the technologies and tools used.

5. To provide installation and execution instructions.

6. To record testing procedures and results.

7. To support future maintenance and improvements.

### 3. Project Overview

EduGenie is a web-based AI-powered educational platform that uses Google Gemini API to assist students in learning.

The application provides:

* AI chatbot for academic doubts.

* Automatic study notes generation.

* Educational content summarization.

* Simple explanations of difficult topics.

* Exam preparation questions and answers.

* Interactive and user-friendly interface.

